Station T-24 (Survey Area T) consists of a six-layer sequence. The resistivity begins at 1101.7 ohm-m, increases slightly in layer 2, and then decreases through layers 3 and 4 to a minimum of 173.3 ohm-m. A significant increase to 2079.8 ohm-m is observed in layer 5, before the resistivity drops again in layer 6. 

Please note that the current file classification of an A-type curve is incorrect based on the interpreted resistivity values; the actual calculated curve type is KQHK. Drilling teams should be prepared for a high-resistivity zone beginning at a depth of 24.89 m.

